\": \"https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/family-game-night-wheel-spinner#faq\",\n      \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How many entries can I add to the wheel for game night?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Most family game nights use between 4 and 20 entries, depending on whether you are picking players, categories or games, though the wheel supports up to 500 entries and resizes its slices automatically.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can I use it on a TV screen during game night?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. Cast your browser to a smart TV or connect a laptop by HDMI, then switch to fullscreen so the whole room can watch the spin together.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What if the same player keeps getting picked repeatedly?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Turn on remove after spin. Each selected entry comes off the wheel once picked, so everyone gets a turn before anyone repeats.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can I give certain family members better odds?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. Tap the built-in + button beside any player's name to weight it from 1x up to 20x—giving a younger or newer player double (2x) or triple (3x) odds cleanly without cluttering the wheel with duplicate lines.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How do I keep forfeits kind for young children?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Let the kids help write the forfeit list and keep it to silly, quick actions such as a funny walk, a song line or ten jumping jacks. Avoid anything embarrassing, and let any player pass and spin again.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Are there other wheel types worth using beyond the standard one?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. A Yes or No wheel is a quick companion for binary calls such as whether to take a break, and a number picker or letter picker can power guessing and word rounds.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"} />

