          <h2 id="schedule">A Sample 90-Minute Game Night</h2>
          <p>
            If you are not sure how to string the ideas together, here is a
            simple run of show you can copy and adjust.
          </p>
          <ol class="plain">
            <li>
              <strong>0:00 · Dinner wheel (Idea 9).</strong> Spin for the meal,
              or the snack wheel if you are eating separately.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>0:15 · Turn order and teams (Ideas 7 and 13).</strong>
              Set both in one minute with "remove after spin."
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>0:20 · Main game (Ideas 4, 6 or 8).</strong> Trivia or a
              spin-picked board game for about 30 minutes.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>0:50 · Break with a quick extra (Ideas 15–20).</strong>
              Letter round or scavenger hunt to get everyone moving.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>1:05 · Creative round (Ideas 3 or 14).</strong> Drawing
              prompts or story round robin as a lower-pressure finale.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>1:20 · Prize draw and movie pick (Ideas 12 and 10).</strong>
              Close with the prize wheel and spin for the movie.
            </li>
          </ol>

